cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the ASR-survival benchmark, please cite it as below. The DIHANA corpus must be cited separately (CC BY 4.0)."
title: "MRCD: multimodal contextual recognition engine for speech disfluencies in Spanish (with the ASR-survival benchmark)"
type: software
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/oratorIA-ProyectoTesis/MRCD"
abstract: "Open-source engine for detecting filler words, prolongations and repetitions in Spanish speech, plus a reusable benchmark (benchmarks/asr_survival) that measures how much human-annotated disfluency evidence survives in ASR transcripts of a 1,025-turn DIHANA frame."
keywords:
  - disfluency
  - speech
  - Spanish
  - ASR
  - benchmark
authors:
